  oilSpecification: "0W-20 or 5W-30 Synthetic (MB 229.71 / MB 229.61)",

  commonIssues: [
    "48V Integrated Starter Generator (ISG) System Failure: The 48V mild-hybrid system is the most common source of faults across all M254 variants. Symptoms include start-stop deactivation, EQ Boost warnings, hybrid system fault memory, and in extreme cases complete 48V battery or ISG failure. The ISG is crankshaft-mounted and requires transmission removal. Costs are very high.",
    "Gasoline Particulate Filter (GPF) Clogging: The GPF requires sustained highway driving for passive regeneration. The higher output of the CLE 300 can load the GPF faster during aggressive urban driving. Frequent short trips cause soot accumulation, limp mode, and performance derating.",
    "Electric Coolant Pump Failures: Three separate electric pumps control engine, turbo, and cabin heating circuits. Failures trigger P0A05, P00B7, and P0C73 codes. Bleeding requires XENTRY diagnostics. Symptoms include temperature warnings and irregular heating.",
    "Exhaust Valve and Guide Defects (Early Production): 2021-2023 production suffered defective exhaust valves causing misfires and cylinder head damage. Mercedes USA extended warranty to 15 years/150,000 miles. Symptoms include severe misfires and power loss.",
    "Elevated Oil Consumption (Early Production): Some early engines consumed oil above spec due to piston ring sealing issues, resolved in later production but relevant for early-build CLE models.",
    "Thermal Management Module Leaks: The electronic coolant distribution module and plastic housings leak or fail electrically, causing erratic temperatures and overheating risk.",
    "Rear Timing Chain Wear: The single-row rear chain is sensitive to oil quality. At 258 hp and 400 Nm, the chain and tensioner face greater stress than the 204 hp variant. Delayed oil changes or incorrect viscosity accelerate wear.",
    "Ground Cable and Electrical Gremlins: Misrouted ground cables cause sporadic ESP, ADAS, and cruise control failures. The dense electronic architecture means small harness issues cascade across domains.",
    "MBUX and Software Glitches: MBUX crashes, restarts, and connectivity issues reflect the platform's software complexity and can mask powertrain diagnostics.",
    "Intercooler Heat Soak: During sustained high-boost driving, the stock intercooler can heat soak, reducing power and increasing combustion temperatures. More noticeable on the 258 hp variant than the 204 hp."
  ],

  vulnerabilities: [
    "48V Mild-Hybrid System Complexity: The ISG and 48V battery are not conventional starter/alternator replacements but complex motor-generators integrated into the powertrain. Their failure affects performance, start-stop, and energy recuperation. Repair requires specialized knowledge and parts, with limited aftermarket support.",
    "GPF Sensitivity at Higher Output: The 258 hp calibration generates more particulate matter than the 204 hp variant under load, accelerating GPF loading. Short-trip driving is even more structurally damaging on the CLE 300 because the filter never reaches sustained regeneration temperatures. Urban-only owners will face GPF issues sooner.",
    "Oil Quality and Timing Chain Stress: The rear single-row chain has minimal safety margin at 400 Nm. Incorrect oil specification or extended intervals cause accelerated stretch. Because the chain is rear-mounted, replacement is a major repair costing thousands.",
    "Cooling System Electronic Fragility: Three electric pumps plus an electronic thermal module create multiple high-failure-probability components. The higher thermal load of the 258 hp calibration stresses the cooling system more than the 204 hp baseline. Any cooling disruption causes immediate power reduction and potential turbo damage.",
    "Direct Injection Carbon Buildup: Without port injection to wash valves, carbon deposits accumulate on intake valve backs, causing rough idle and misfires. The higher output variant may accumulate deposits slightly faster due to richer mixtures under boost.",
    "Early Production Defects: 2021-2023 build dates carry exhaust valve/guide and oil consumption risks. A CLE 300 from early production should have dealer service history confirming any warranty campaigns were performed.",
    "Turbocharger Thermal Stress: The higher boost pressures of the 258 hp calibration push the twin-scroll turbo near its continuous thermal limit. Sustained autobahn driving or mountain passes place extreme thermal load on the bearing housing and wastegate actuator. Oil coking from hot shutdowns is a real risk.",
    "Dealer Dependency and Diagnostic Complexity: The M254 requires XENTRY for bleeding, ISG calibration, ECU updates, and GPF service. Independent garages without Mercedes-specific tools cannot properly maintain this engine. Ownership costs are inflated by this dependency.",
    "Intercooler and Boost Path Integrity: The higher boost pressures stress intercooler hoses, plastic pipes, and clamps. Aging or heat-cycled connectors can split, causing unmetered air leaks, underboost, and potential lean-running damage to pistons or GPF."
  ],

