  oilSpecification: "0W-20 or 5W-30 Synthetic (MB 229.71 / MB 229.61 / API SP)",

  commonIssues: [
    "48V Integrated Starter Generator (ISG) System Failure: Identical to European variant. The 48V mild-hybrid system is the dominant failure source. Symptoms include disabled start-stop, EQ Boost warnings, hybrid fault codes, and eventual ISG or 48V battery replacement. The ISG requires transmission removal. Costs in North America are typically 3,000-6,000 USD depending on labor rates.",
    "Gasoline Particulate Filter (GPF) Clogging: The North American CLE 300 4MATIC is equipped with a GPF for EPA/CARB compliance. While US highway driving patterns generally favor passive regeneration, urban owners in stop-and-go traffic or cold climates experience the same soot loading and limp mode as European owners. The higher 255 hp output loads the GPF marginally faster than the 204 hp CLE 200.",
    "Electric Coolant Pump Failures: Three electric pumps (engine, turbo, heater) fail with the same P0A05, P00B7, and P0C73 fault codes. XENTRY is required for cooling system bleeding after replacement. Independent shops without Mercedes diagnostics cannot complete this repair properly.",
    "Exhaust Valve and Guide Defects (Early Production): The North American market received the same early M254 production with defective exhaust valves. Mercedes USA extended warranty coverage to 15 years/150,000 miles. Symptoms include severe misfires, flashing MIL, and power loss. Any 2021-2023 build date CLE 300 should have VIN-checked service campaigns.",
    "Elevated Oil Consumption (Early Production): Early M254 engines showed oil consumption above 1.0L/1,000 miles in some cases due to piston ring sealing issues. This appears resolved in later production but remains relevant for early-build inventory.",
    "Thermal Management Module Leaks: The electronic thermal management module and plastic coolant distribution housings leak or suffer electronic actuator failure, causing erratic temperatures and overheating warnings.",
    "Rear Timing Chain Wear: The single-row rear chain is equally sensitive in North American service. The 400 Nm torque and cold-start thermal cycling in winter climates stress the chain and tensioner. Oil quality is paramount; deviations from MB 229.71 accelerate wear.",
    "4MATIC Transfer Case and Front Differential: The CLE 300 4MATIC adds a transfer case and front differential that require fluid service every 60,000 km/40,000 miles. Neglect causes shudder, binding on tight turns, and premature clutch pack wear. The 4MATIC system adds approximately 80 kg of unsprung and driveline mass, increasing fuel consumption and wear rates.",
    "MBUX and Software Glitches: North American MBUX systems experience the same crashes, restarts, and connectivity issues as European models. Over-the-air updates help but do not eliminate all software instability.",
    "Ground Cable and ADAS Faults: Misrouted ground cables cause the same sporadic ESP, lane-keeping, and cruise control failures reported in European models."
  ],

  vulnerabilities: [
    "48V Mild-Hybrid System Complexity: The ISG and 48V lithium battery are the same complex motor-generator architecture as the European variant. North American labor rates and parts pricing make replacement even more expensive than in Europe. Independent repair infrastructure for the 48V system is severely limited in the US and Canada.",
    "GPF and EPA/CARB Compliance: The North American GPF is functionally identical to the European unit and equally sensitive to driving patterns. Cold climates compound the problem because the engine takes longer to reach regeneration temperatures. Any modifications that disable or remove the GPF violate federal emissions law and trigger warranty voidance.",
    "Oil Quality and Extended Drain Intervals: North American dealers often promote 10,000-mile (16,000 km) oil change intervals under 'Assyst Plus' service plans. For the M254, this is at the upper limit of safety for the rear timing chain. Severe service (short trips, cold climate, stop-and-go) demands 5,000-7,500-mile intervals with the exact specified low-ash synthetic oil.",
    "Cooling System Electronic Fragility: The three electric pumps and electronic thermal module are identical to European specification and equally prone to failure. North American summer heat and winter cold extremes stress these components more than temperate European climates.",
    "4MATIC Driveline Maintenance Burden: The all-wheel-drive system adds transfer case fluid, front differential fluid, and additional driveshaft components that require periodic service. The 4MATIC clutch pack can bind or shudder if fluid is degraded, and the front axle increases tire wear costs.",
    "Direct Injection Carbon Buildup: Without port fuel injection, intake valve carbon accumulation is inevitable. North American gasoline quality varies dramatically; top-tier detergent gasoline (Top Tier) delays carbon buildup, while discount fuel accelerates it. Walnut blasting or chemical cleaning is required typically every 80,000-100,000 km (50,000-60,000 miles).",
    "Early Production Defects: North American 2021-2023 build dates carry the same exhaust valve/guide and oil consumption risks. The Mercedes USA warranty extension is valuable but requires dealer verification. Private sales of early-build cars without confirmed campaign completion are high-risk.",
    "Dealer Dependency and Diagnostic Cost: XENTRY diagnostics are required for cooling system bleeding, ISG calibration, ECU updates, and 4MATIC clutch pack adaptation. Independent shops without Mercedes factory tools cannot perform these procedures. North American dealer labor rates (150-250 USD/hour) make even routine diagnostics expensive.",
    "Turbocharger Thermal Stress: The 255 hp calibration pushes the twin-scroll turbo to the same thermal limits as the 258 hp European variant. Sustained high-speed Interstate driving, mountain grades, and hot ambient temperatures place severe thermal load on the bearing housing. Oil coking from immediate shutdown after hard driving is a documented risk.",
    "Winter Cold-Start Wear: The 48V ISG enables exceptionally smooth cold starts, but the aluminum block and direct injection system experience accelerated wear during frequent sub-zero cold starts without adequate warm-up. The 48V battery also suffers reduced capacity and longevity in extreme cold climates."
  ],

