  "oilSpecification": "10W-40, 5W-40, or 5W-30 Synthetic or Semi-Synthetic (API SL/SM, MB 229.1 / 229.3)",

  "commonIssues": [
    "Biodegradable Wiring Harness Degradation: The most critical and famous issue affecting all 1993-2000 Mercedes engines, equally present in overseas-market vehicles. The engine wiring harness insulation is made from biodegradable soy-based plastic that flakes and crumbles, exposing bare copper wire. This causes misfires, hard starting, stalling, rough idle, HFM sensor faults, and can short-circuit the ECU. The entire engine harness must be replaced or rebuilt with modern wire. This is not an 'if' but a 'when' failure on any pre-facelift CLK 200 that has not had its harness replaced.",
    "HFM (Hot Film Mass) Sensor Failure: The airflow sensor mounted on the intake tube is prone to contamination, aging, and wiring harness-related faults. A failed HFM sensor causes incorrect mixture calculations, resulting in poor acceleration, rough idle, and fault codes. Cleaning with dedicated MAF sensor cleaner can restore function; replacement is straightforward.",
    "Camshaft Adjuster (Variable Valve Timing) Leak and Rattle: The intake camshaft adjuster is controlled by a solenoid and can leak oil from its seals. Internal wear causes a characteristic deep rattling noise at idle. The adjuster and its solenoid valve are known wear items. Replacement of the adjuster unit and solenoid resolves the issue.",
    "Timing Chain Stretch and Tensioner Wear: The simplex (single-row) timing chain stretches over time, particularly with extended oil change intervals. The hydraulic tensioner reaches its travel limit and cannot maintain tension, causing a rattle on startup. In severe cases, the chain can jump teeth, causing valve-to-piston contact and catastrophic engine damage. Preventive chain and tensioner replacement at 150,000-180,000 km is recommended.",
    "Oil Leaks (Valve Cover Gasket, Cam Adjuster Seals, Oil Pan): The aluminum valve cover gasket hardens and leaks oil onto the exhaust manifold, creating smoke and odor. The camshaft adjuster seals and front crankshaft seal are also common leak points. The oil pan gasket weeps with age. These are nuisance leaks but indicate the engine's age.",
    "Coolant Loss (Head Gasket, Water Pump, Expansion Tank): The head gasket can develop external leaks between cylinders 1-2 or 3-4, causing coolant loss without mixing into the oil. The plastic expansion tank cracks with age. The water pump weeps from the bearing seal. The heater control valve (if equipped) leaks coolant into the interior.",
    "Idle Air Control / Throttle Body Issues: The electronic throttle body or idle air control valve accumulates carbon and fails to maintain stable idle. This causes erratic idle speed, stalling, and poor cold-start behavior. Cleaning or replacement is effective.",
    "Ignition Coil and Spark Plug Wire Degradation: The pencil-type ignition coils mounted directly on the spark plugs can fail, causing misfires. Coil failure is more likely on engines with original wiring harness degradation because voltage irregularities stress the coils.",
    "Engine Mounts: The hydraulic engine mounts collapse with age, transmitting excessive vibration to the cabin and causing harsh shifting due to engine movement. Replacement restores refinement.",
    "Exhaust Flex Pipe and Catalytic Converter: The flex pipe in the front exhaust section cracks, causing leaks and noise. The catalytic converter can clog after 200,000+ km, causing backpressure, power loss, and overheating."
  ],

  "vulnerabilities": [
    "Wiring Harness as an Existential Threat: The biodegradable wiring harness is not merely an inconvenience; it is a safety and drivability issue that can destroy the ECU, cause stalls in traffic, and create intermittent faults that are maddening to diagnose. Any prospective buyer must verify that the engine harness has been replaced with a modern, non-biodegradable unit or professionally rebuilt. A pre-facelift CLK 200 with an original harness is a guaranteed problem. The cost of a replacement harness or professional rebuild is 400-800 EUR (or local market equivalent), which is a significant percentage of the car's value but absolutely non-negotiable.",
    "Timing Chain as a Catastrophic Failure Point: While the timing chain is generally durable, a neglected chain that stretches beyond the tensioner's capacity can jump teeth. Because the M111 is an interference engine, a jumped chain causes valve-to-piston contact, bending valves and potentially damaging pistons. This transforms a 500 EUR preventive repair into a 2,000-3,000 EUR engine rebuild. The symptoms (startup rattle, rough idle) are easy to detect if the owner is attentive; the danger is the owner who ignores the noise until failure.",
    "Parts Availability and Aging Components: At nearly 30 years old, rubber components, plastic connectors, sensors, and gaskets are aging regardless of mileage. The plastic coolant expansion tank, radiator tanks, vacuum lines, and various connectors become brittle. In overseas markets (South Africa, Australia, Southeast Asia), parts availability may be better or worse than Europe depending on local Mercedes dismantler networks and aftermarket support.",
    "HFM Sensor Dependence: The engine's entire fuel injection strategy depends on the HFM sensor. When it fails or reads inaccurately, the engine runs poorly. While the sensor is not expensive, diagnosing HFM-related issues requires understanding that wiring harness faults can mimic sensor failure. Many unnecessary HFM sensors are replaced when the real culprit is the harness.",
    "Oil Consumption from Valve Seals: With age, the valve stem seals harden and allow oil to seep into the combustion chambers during vacuum events (deceleration, idle). This causes blue smoke on startup, oil consumption, and catalytic converter fouling. Replacement requires removal of the camshafts and is a 600-900 EUR repair.",
    "Corrosion in Subframe and Structural Elements: The C208 CLK, while better protected than earlier Mercedes models, is now old enough that rust in the front subframe, floor pans, jack points, and wheel arches is a concern. In coastal or humid overseas markets (Durban, Sydney, Southeast Asia), corrosion may be accelerated compared to European inland climates.",
    "ECU Heat and Moisture Exposure: The ME-SFI ECU is mounted in the engine bay and can suffer from solder joint cracks due to thermal cycling. In hot overseas climates, ECU thermal stress is higher than in temperate Europe. This causes intermittent faults that are difficult to trace.",
    "Brake System Age: The ABS system (Bosch 5.3 or 5.7 depending on year) can suffer from pump motor failure, relay issues, or wheel speed sensor faults. The brake lines may corrode internally.",
    "Transmission (722.6 or Manual): The 5-speed automatic (722.6 5G-Tronic) is generally durable but requires fluid and filter service every 60,000 km. The 13-pin connector to the transmission leaks fluid into the wiring, causing conductor plate and shift solenoid issues. The manual transmission is robust but the clutch and release bearing are wear items.",
    "Market Value vs. Repair Cost Economics: The CLK C208 is now an affordable classic. This creates an economic trap where a 2,000 EUR engine repair (harness, chain, head gasket) exceeds 50% of the car's value. Owners must be prepared for this reality or choose to perform their own maintenance."
  ],

