          "HFM Sensor as a Drivability Critical Point: A failed HFM sensor causes significant mixture errors on a V8 that moves large air volumes.",
          "Cooling System Sensitivity: The all-aluminum construction is less forgiving of overheating than iron-block engines.",
          "Age-Stacked Ownership Costs: Multiple medium-cost jobs accumulate on a 20-plus-year-old V8 Mercedes.",
