            "Mass Air Flow Sensor Degradation: A tired MAF causes hesitation, soft throttle response, and mixture-related fault behavior.",
            "Oil Cooler and Front Seal Leaks: Age-related leaks from the oil filter housing area and front crank sealing surfaces are common on older M113 engines.",
            "Rear Main Seal Weepage: High-mileage examples may develop persistent oil seepage between engine and transmission.",
            "Engine Mount Collapse: Old hydraulic mounts flatten or leak, causing vibration and making the car feel harsher than it should.",
            "Cooling System Aging: Thermostat, water pump, radiator, expansion tank, and hoses all age out and must not be ignored on an AMG V8.",
            "Electronic Throttle Body Wear: Early electronic throttle hardware can develop wear or intermittent behavior with age.",
            "Crankshaft and Camshaft Position Sensor Failure: Can cause hard starts, intermittent stalling, or rough running.",
