                  "Water Pump Failure: The water pump is often driven by the timing belt and should be replaced preventively during belt service.",
                  "Oil Cooler Seal Leaks: The oil-to-coolant heat exchanger leaks at the gasket interface with age, causing external seepage or coolant contamination.",
                  "Valve Cover Gasket Leaks: The magnesium AMG valve covers can weep oil into spark plug tubes with age and heat cycling.",
                  "Front Crankshaft Seal Leak: The main seal hardens and leaks, particularly on high-mileage engines.",
                  "Rear Main Seal Leak: Can develop with significant mileage, requiring transmission removal for access.",
                  "Engine Mount Collapse: The 510 Nm torque destroys hydraulic engine mounts rapidly, causing driveline shudder and harshness.",
                  "Transmission Mount Wear: The 5G-Tronic is heavy and transmits significant torque, accelerating mount fatigue.",
                  "Cooling System Aging: Expansion tanks, thermostats, water pumps, and hoses degrade under the thermal load of the large-displacement AMG V8.",
                  "Crankcase Ventilation Clogging: Increased pressure forces oil past seals and gaskets.",
